  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Monique. You're verified. I checked the delivery records for each of your recent orders. Here's what I found and what I've done:\n\n**Saffron Lane (K-6501, today):** promised for 6:00 PM, handed to you at 6:52 PM, so 52 minutes late. For deliveries 45 minutes or more late, the credit is 20% of the subtotal, which would be $25.60. As a Plus member, the most you can get for a late delivery is $25. **I've added $25.00 in credit.**\n\n**Pho Real (K-6502, Oct 22):** promised for 7:15 PM, handed to you at 7:45 PM, so 30 minutes late. **I've added $5.00 in credit.**\n\n**Taqueria Luz (K-6503, Oct 20):** at 5:50 PM, we sent you a push notification saying the courier shortage had moved your delivery time to 7:00 PM. The order arrived at 7:12 PM. An order counts as late only if it arrives more than 15 minutes after the delivery time, so this one doesn't qualify for credit.\n\n**Burger Barn (K-6504, Oct 16):** this order was late, but you can only ask for late-delivery credit within 7 days of delivery. That window closed on Oct 23, so I can't give credit for this one.\n\n**Your credit balance is now $30.00.** It will apply to your future orders. Late-delivery compensation is always given as credit, not as a refund to your card.\n\nI'm sorry this week's orders were so frustrating. Is there anything else on your list I can check?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks for going through them. I'd like to ask about Taqueria Luz, though. I didn't see that notification at 5:50, and I was waiting on the order from 6:00 onward. Nobody told me it was moving to 7:00 before that. Is there any way to look into it?\n\nAlso, I'm not sure about the Burger Barn one. I thought I had raised it earlier than Oct 23, but I'll double-check my notes. Can you tell me what date you're counting from?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I looked at both again.\n\n**Taqueria Luz (K-6503):** Our delivery record shows a push notification sent to you at 5:50 PM on Oct 20 that moved your delivery time from 6:30 PM to 7:00 PM because of a courier shortage. The record also confirms it reached you. Under our policy, an update sent at least 30 minutes before the original delivery time becomes the new delivery time, and this one went out 40 minutes before. Measured against 7:00 PM, the order arrived 12 minutes later, so it doesn't count as late. I understand you didn't see the notification, but I have to go by the delivery record, so I can't add credit for this order.\n\n**Burger Barn (K-6504):** I'm counting from when the order was handed to you, which was **Oct 16 at 8:00 PM**. The 7-day window for late-delivery credit ran until **Oct 23 at 8:00 PM**. I also checked your support history, and there are no earlier contacts on file, for this order or any other. If you reached out some other way, it wasn't recorded, so I can't give credit for this order.\n\nI know this isn't what you were hoping for. If you'd like a specialist to review either order, I can pass it to one, and they'll follow up within 24 hours. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, I understand. I'd like the specialist review for Taqueria Luz, please. I never got that notification at 5:50, so I'd like someone to look at whether it actually reached my phone.\n\nFor Burger Barn, I'll check my notes and see whether I contacted you some other way. I'll come back to you if I find something. For now, please leave that one as is.\n\nAlso, I still need to talk about the summer rolls. They were missing from my Pho Real order on Thursday (#6502). Can we sort that out too?"
  },
